From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: qca: run the WCN3991 without in-band sleep

Once the NVM settings were applied (previous patch), the controller
enabled in-band sleep (IBS) and deep sleep. After its first sleep it
never answered the host again: the host sent thousands of HCI_IBS_WAKE_IND
bytes and received no HCI_IBS_WAKE_ACK, so every HCI command timed out
and discovery failed. On Android the Bluetooth HAL handles waking with
UART clock votes (TIOCPMGET/TIOCPMPUT on the downstream msm_geni_serial
driver); hci_qca's clock vote hooks are empty.

Keep the WCN399x out of IBS and deep sleep: do not set the IBS and deep
sleep bits in the NVM for it, and do not enable IBS on the host side.
The controller then stays awake while Bluetooth is powered, which costs
some idle power; turning Bluetooth off still powers it down.

---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-10-24 02:17:13.560076825 +0100
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-10-24 02:17:28.939722194 +0100
@@ -204,9 +204,12 @@
 			case EDL_TAG_ID_HCI:
 				/* HCI transport layer parameters
 				 * enabling software inband sleep
-				 * onto controller side.
+				 * onto controller side. Not on WCN399x:
+				 * hci_qca cannot wake it again through the
+				 * downstream UART driver, see hci_qca.c.
 				 */
-				tlv_nvm->data[0] |= 0x80;
+				if (!config->wcn399x)
+					tlv_nvm->data[0] |= 0x80;
 
 				/* UART Baud Rate: WCN399x keep it one byte
 				 * earlier (mainline 7dc5fe0814c3)
@@ -222,7 +225,8 @@
 				/* Sleep enable mask
 				 * enabling deep sleep feature on controller.
 				 */
-				tlv_nvm->data[0] |= 0x01;
+				if (!config->wcn399x)
+					tlv_nvm->data[0] |= 0x01;
 
 				break;
 			}
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c	2026-10-24 02:17:13.560155386 +0100
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c	2026-10-24 02:17:28.939871966 +0100
@@ -1192,7 +1192,14 @@
 	/* Setup patch / NVM configurations */
 	ret = qca_uart_setup(hdev, qca_baudrate, qcadev->btsoc_type, soc_ver);
 	if (!ret) {
-		set_bit(STATE_IN_BAND_SLEEP_ENABLED, &qca->flags);
+		/* The WCN3990/WCN3991 setup leaves in-band sleep off in the
+		 * NVM: on Android the Bluetooth HAL wakes the controller with
+		 * UART clock votes this driver does not make, and with IBS on
+		 * the controller stopped answering wake requests after its
+		 * first sleep.
+		 */
+		if (qcadev->btsoc_type != QCA_WCN3990)
+			set_bit(STATE_IN_BAND_SLEEP_ENABLED, &qca->flags);
 		qca_debugfs_init(hdev);
 	} else if (ret == -ENOENT) {
 		/* No patch/nvm-config found, run with original fw/config */
